*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Molecule: N2
* Basis: cc-pVDZ
* Symmetry: C2
* Features tested: RASSCF(SA, unequal weights), MCLR(internal state rotations), ALASKA
* Responsible person: Roland Lindh
* Comments: Unequally weighted SA-CASSCF over two exactly degenerate 1Pi pairs
*           (both components of each pair belong to irrep b in C2). The internal
*           state rotations are then solved iteratively, and their preconditioner
*           must not divide by the vanishing energy difference of the degenerate
*           states (the Z-vector equations used to diverge). The analytical
*           gradient agrees with the numerical one (0.34647 for N1, z).
*           The multipole moments of the individual Pi states depend on the
*           arbitrary rotation within each degenerate pair, so they are not
*           checked.
*-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
>> export MOLCAS_NOCHECK=MLTPL

&GATEWAY
  Coord = 2
    N2
    N   0.000000   0.000000  -0.550000
    N   0.000000   0.000000   0.550000
  Basis = cc-pVDZ
  Group = XY
  NoCD

&SEWARD

&SCF

&RASSCF
  Symmetry = 2
  nActEl = 10 0 0
  Inactive = 2 0
  Ras2 = 4 4
  CIRoot = 4 4
    1 2 3 4
    3 3 1 1
  RlxRoot = 1
  Thrs = 1.0e-10 1.0e-06 1.0e-06

&MCLR
  Threshold = 1.0e-6

&ALASKA
